From d415cd6b8f31e24fd3409bca4a19ba893a33b38e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Orbit Dev <dev@orbit.invalid>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 17:58:24 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 15/31] feat(orbit): /orbit/status and /orbit/events long-poll
 on the HTTPS API

StatusTracker polls a StatusSource every 500 ms (only while clients are
active), bumps seq on change and answers long-poll waiters on change or
timeout (max 25 s, one pending per client uuid; a new wait answers the old).
Responses are held asynchronously. Windows source: foreground window title
and process name, Core Audio master volume/mute, SMTC media via C++/WinRT;
failures leave fields empty. Routes require the view permission and are
registered only on the mTLS server.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
